      "title": "M1.4 · W1: audio → score with Orchidea",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "W1 (Phase 1): a sound is orchestrated by Orchidea into a score for ensemble.\n\nNeeds: TinySOL in models/m5/orchidea_db/TinySOL (folder holding TinySOL.spectrum.db and the TinySOL/ samples). Download: https://www.orch-idea.org/datasets/ (a symlink works). Restart ComfyUI or press R, then pick it in Orchidea's \"database\" dropdown.\n\nPress Run (~1 s on this 1 s 440 Hz sine). Look at:\n1. Score Viewer: the orchestration quantized to a score, one staff per instrument, notes around A4.\n2. Sequence Viewer: the same notes unquantized, at their real onset times.\n3. The two players: Orchidea's own rendering (with reverb) and m5's mix of the same samples (dry). They should sound alike.\n\nTry: change \"orchestra\" (e.g. \"Fl Ob ClBb Vn Vc\"), set styles to \"ord\" or dynamics to \"pp p\", raise sparsity to 0.1 for fewer instruments, turn reverb off. \"Show advanced inputs\" reveals segmentation, onsets_timegate, pop_size, max_epochs. Swap the sine for any WAV in input/ (e.g. a chord or a bell) via Load Audio."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
